      "message": "Seems like the domain type can changed at runtime from DMA to DMA-FQ with devices still bound:\n```\n*\n * Changing the default domain through sysfs requires the users to unbind the\n * drivers from the devices in the iommu group, except for a DMA -\u003e DMA-FQ\n * transition. Return failure if this isn\u0027t met.\n *\n * We need to consider the race between this and the device release path.\n * group-\u003emutex is used here to guarantee that the device release path\n * will not be entered at the same time.\n */\nstatic ssize_t iommu_group_store_type(struct iommu_group *group,\n»       »       »       »             const char *buf, size_t count)\n...\n...\n»       /* We can bring up a flush queue without tearing down the domain. */\n»       if (req_type \u003d\u003d IOMMU_DOMAIN_DMA_FQ \u0026\u0026\n»           group-\u003edefault_domain-\u003etype \u003d\u003d IOMMU_DOMAIN_DMA) {\n```\n\nThats the reason I thought I will pass it with every unmap call. Even if the host spoofs this to be a DMA_FQ while its actually in strict mode, donation API is supposed to flush the caches and we should be safe I guess.",
